# quietm-uart under qemu-system-mips -- 2026-08-29, RUNSHEET P3

# the eight boot marks, and B07 with a value

host        Linux 6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2
qemu        QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18)
tool        tools/deskchan.py 1.0   (NOT tools/rlxprobe/qemu-run.sh --
            different entry mechanism, different CPU, different UART;
            qemu/README.md says which is which and why it matters)
machine     -M malta -m 128 -cpu 4Kc -bios <4-instruction stub>
            -device loader,file=<image>,addr=0,force-raw=on
            -serial null -serial null -serial file:   (index 2 = CBUS)
seconds     30 (nothing here halts; the run is bounded by timeout)

## the DEVICE artefact this run is about
    vmlinux    3968240 bytes  sha256 dd0c1190f364656107a86248d87a75cdc5403dde08ab05b020da275a78fc4b08
    nfjrom     1027072 bytes  sha256 cf8a93d73025292ddc61f28c7172ad00985efad8569bdfbcae69def3a10dfb8a   <- what gets uploaded
    entry      0x80003600   (kernelStartAddr, read out of the nfjrom header)

## the qemu image -- NOT the same bytes
    decompressed image 3472384 bytes  sha256 e084038dc0dc16d5150acb543417f6dffda05749beedfede6ac944a2ec69d7ea
    Two declared patches, and nothing else:
      COP3 -> nop   4 word(s) -> nop: 0x8000233C(4c880000) 0x8000234C(4c880800) 0x80002398(4c882000) 0x800023A8(4c882800)
                    qemu 4Kc raises Coprocessor Unusable on these; the
                    channel therefore SKIPS the Lexra IMEM/DMEM setup
      UART          prom_putchar 0x8000B088+100 -> 5 word(s): 3c02b800 x2 34462014 x1 34452008 x1 34422000 x1
                    0xB8002000/08/14 -> 0xBF000900/10/28, malta CBUS.
                    Five words inside prom_putchar, window from the
                    symbol table. On the device none of this is present.

